@scene chapter_5_locked_grimoire

background: ancient_library.png
music: wisdom_theme.mp3

dialogue:
"The road climbs to a squat stone archive, half-swallowed by ivy."
"Inside, shelves run off in every direction, and not one of them is in any order you can see."
"An old woman sits at the centre, eyes clouded white, her hands moving over a great locked book as though reading a face."

background: cataloguer

npc Cataloguer:
"Come in, come in. Mind the third shelf — it bites."
"You're the one Gruff sent. He counts from zero. I don't count at all."

npc You:
"You're... blind. How do you find anything in here?"

npc Cataloguer:
"By its NAME, child. Never by where it sits."

system notification:
"NEW QUEST"
"THE LOCKED GRIMOIRE"
"Open the spellbook that answers only to names."

npc Cataloguer:
"Your Quartermaster's satchels are fine things — if you can SEE which slot you want."
"But I cannot. Numbers on a shelf are no use to a blind woman."
"So I keep my knowledge another way. Not a line — a set of PAIRS."
"Every spell has a name, and every name points to its incantation."

dialogue:
"She lays her palm flat on the grimoire. Its iron lock clicks open."

npc Cataloguer:
"That is a dictionary, traveller. You never ask it 'what is in slot two?'"
"You ask it 'what answers to the name FIRE?' — and it hands you the answer, wherever the thing happens to sit."
"A key. A value. Say the key; receive the value."

npc Cataloguer:
"But be gentle with it. Ask for a name the book does not hold, and a lesser book would shriek and slam its covers shut."
"Mine is kinder — if you ask it kindly. Ask with GET, and hand it a word to say when it knows nothing."
"Then a missing spell is not a catastrophe. It is only a shrug."

dialogue:
"She slides the open grimoire toward you. Names shimmer along its margins, each tied by a thread of light to an incantation somewhere in the pages."

npc Cataloguer:
"A traveller will name the spell they need. Fetch its incantation by that name."
"And if the book has never held it — do not let it scream. Have it answer 'Unknown Spell,' and move on."

system system:
"MISSION"
"Look up a spell by name. Use .get so an unknown name returns 'Unknown Spell' instead of crashing."

mission: grimoire_dicts

dialogue:
"You speak a name. A thread of light pulls taut, and the matching incantation rises off the page and hangs glowing in the air."
"Then you speak a name the book has never held — and instead of shrieking, it simply murmurs, 'Unknown Spell,' and waits."
"The Cataloguer smiles at the sound."

npc Cataloguer:
"There. You've learned to ask by name — and to ask kindly."
"That second part matters more than the first. The Blight, when you get right down to it, is only unhandled screaming."
"Go west, to the old loom. A weaver waits there who speaks in nothing but riddles."
"She'll teach your words to bend. You'll need it — the lazy one on the mountain won't repeat himself."

system level_up:
"CHAPTER COMPLETE"
"The Locked Grimoire"
"Applied: dictionaries · key → value · .get with a default"

reward:
xp: 100
gold: 50
achievement: SPEAKER OF NAMES

next:
chapter_5b_card_catalogue
